{%- comment -%}
  Product card. Shared by the shop grid and the collection rows so there is one
  implementation to fix, not two.
  Params: product (required)

  v2 (Dani's 2026-08-31 direction). She called out David Protein's product cards
  specifically: the card should answer "what is it and why is it good for me" before
  you click. So the card now carries the macro strip (protein / calories / sugar) and
  up to two claim chips, straight from the `prodani` metafields.

  Two rules this snippet will not break:
    - **Macros render only when the metafield is actually set.** No sample numbers on
      a grid — the PDP can flag a sample in context, a card cannot, and a made-up
      macro is a nutrition claim.
    - **Claim chips are never inferred.** A chip appears only when its boolean is
      explicitly true in admin (ticket T2). Nothing is derived from the title or
      collection, because "it says gluten free in the name" is not substantiation.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture handles -%}
  {%- for c in product.collections -%}{{ c.handle }} {% endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign cat = '' -%}
{%- for c in product.collections -%}
  {%- if cat == '' and c.handle != 'all-products' -%}{%- assign cat = c.title -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- liquid
  assign mf = product.metafields.prodani
  assign protein = mf.protein_g.value
  assign calories = mf.calories.value
  assign sugar = mf.sugar_g.value
  assign has_macros = false
  if protein != blank or calories != blank or sugar != blank
    assign has_macros = true
  endif
-%}

<a class="pd-card{% if product.images.size < 2 %} pd-card--single{% endif %}"
   href="{{ product.url }}" data-pd-item data-collections="{{ handles | strip }}">
  <div class="pd-card__media">
    {%- if product.featured_image != blank -%}
      {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 800
         | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', class: 'pd-card__img pd-card__img--main',
           alt: product.title,
           sizes: '(min-width:1181px) 22vw, (min-width:821px) 30vw, 46vw',
           widths: '300, 450, 600, 800' }}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if product.images[1] != blank -%}
      {{ product.images[1] | image_url: width: 800
         | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', class: 'pd-card__img pd-card__img--alt', alt: '' }}
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="pd-card__badges">
      {%- unless product.available -%}<span class="pd-badge pd-badge--out">Sold out</span>{%- endunless -%}
      {%- if handles contains 'vegan' -%}<span class="pd-badge pd-badge--vegan">Vegan</span>{%- endif -%}
    </div>
    <span class="pd-card__quick">View treat</span>
  </div>

  <p class="pd-card__cat">{{ cat | default: 'Treat' | escape }}</p>
  <h3 class="pd-card__name">{{ product.title | escape }}</h3>

  {%- comment -%}
    Macro strip — the "why it's good for me", on the card face. Each cell only
    appears when its own value is set, so a half-filled product degrades to a
    shorter strip rather than to zeroes.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if has_macros -%}
    <ul class="pd-card__macros" aria-label="Nutrition per cake">
      {%- if protein != blank -%}
        <li><b>{{ protein }}g</b><span>protein</span></li>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if calories != blank -%}
        <li><b>{{ calories }}</b><span>cal</span></li>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if sugar != blank -%}
        <li><b>{{ sugar }}g</b><span>sugar</span></li>
      {%- endif -%}
    </ul>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Claim chips — capped at two so the card stays a card. Order is deliberate:
    the two claims Dani leads the brand on come first.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign chips = ''
    if mf.no_sugar_added.value == true
      assign chips = chips | append: 'No added sugar|'
    endif
    if mf.gluten_free.value == true
      assign chips = chips | append: 'Gluten free|'
    endif
    if mf.high_protein.value == true
      assign chips = chips | append: 'High protein|'
    endif
    if mf.high_fiber.value == true
      assign chips = chips | append: 'High fiber|'
    endif
    assign chiplist = chips | split: '|'
  -%}
  {%- if chiplist.size > 0 -%}
    <ul class="pd-card__chips">
      {%- for chip in chiplist limit: 2 -%}
        <li>{{ chip }}</li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  {%- endif -%}

  <p class="pd-card__price">
    {{- product.price | money -}}
    {%- render 'prodani-pack-price', variant: product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
  </p>
</a>
